<%# Google's inline booking page for the app's appointment schedule
    (Studio.booking_url). Rendered by `studio_booking_frame`. It fills its
    container, so it lines up with the cards around it. Google lays it out by
    width: month beside the slots from about 600px, stacked below that. It
    cannot be themed, so it sits on a white panel in both themes.

    CROPPED AT REST, WHOLE IN USE. From 640px up the wrapper shows only the
    "Select an appointment time" box: Google's header above it and its credit
    lines below are clipped (measured in the frame at 640-862px wide: the box
    spans 211-613px of a 732px page). The crop cannot stay on, because the form
    that opens when a slot is picked is a dialog centred in the frame's FULL
    height (93-640px), so a cropped frame cuts off its title and its Book
    button. A cross-origin frame reports no clicks, but the parent window does
    lose focus to it; on that signal the wrapper opens to the full frame.
    Below 640px Google stacks the month above the slots and nothing is cropped.
    Those numbers are Google's layout, measured 2026-09-30; `crop: false` drops
    the crop if that layout moves.

    THE SRC IS DEFERRED, and not with loading="lazy". The frame is a third
    party, and a frame that starts loading before the window's `load` event
    holds that event open for as long as Google takes to answer. So the URL
    waits in data-src and the script in studio/booking/_assets assigns it only
    AFTER `load`, once the frame is near the viewport.

    WITH SCRIPTS OFF nothing ever assigns the src, so the <noscript> hides the
    empty frame and puts a plain link to Google's booking page in its place. %>
<%= studio_booking_assets %>
<div class="booking-frame<%= " booking-frame-cropped" if crop %>" data-booking-wrap>
  <iframe data-booking-frame
          data-src="<%= studio_booking_embed_url %>"
          title="<%= title %>"
          width="100%" frameborder="0"></iframe>
  <noscript>
    <style>.booking-frame { height: auto !important; } .booking-frame iframe { display: none !important; }</style>
    <p class="booking-frame-noscript"><a href="<%= Studio.booking_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the booking page to pick a time</a></p>
  </noscript>
</div>
<p class="booking-frame-note">
  Scheduling by Google Calendar. Trouble seeing it?
  <a href="<%= Studio.booking_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the booking page</a>.
</p>
